    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31563" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏaxes</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏaxis</span></b> , is, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄαξις</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river in Crete</i>, now <i>Axus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rapidum Cretae veniemus Oaxen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 1, 66</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏaxis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f.
			<i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the
				Oaxes;</i>
			<b>poet.</b> for <i>Cretan</i>:
			capiens tellurem Oaxida, Varr. Atacin. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. E. 1, 66</span></i>.</div>
